---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import fixture from './fixture.json';
import provenance from './provenance.json';
import './listening.css';
const story = fixture.aligned.map(word => word.word).join(' ');
---
<section class="ll" aria-labelledby="ll-title">
  <div class="ll-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">An original story / A working player</p><h2 id="ll-title">Find the phrase.<br /><em>Hear it again.</em></h2></div><p>Play the story, follow the words, then choose a passage to repeat. The sound and waveform are the same original sample used in the recordings below.</p></div>
  <div class="ll-disclosure"><Icon name="play" /><p><strong>AI-generated Danish narration.</strong> Standard Cedar voice · 15.9 seconds · an original fictional story.</p></div>
  <div data-listening-mount id="ll-player"><div class="ll-fallback"><p class="ll-fallback-basic">Play the original sample. Enable JavaScript for word highlighting, waveform seeking and phrase loops.</p><p class="ll-fallback-loading" role="status">Loading the word and waveform player. You can already play the original sample below.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="/media/listening/sample.wav" aria-label="Original Danish story, AI-generated Cedar narration"></audio></div></div>
  <script is:inline>document.currentScript?.previousElementSibling?.setAttribute('data-listening-enhanced', '');</script>
  <details class="ll-transcript" id="ll-story"><summary>Read the complete original Danish story</summary><p lang="da">{story}</p></details>
  <p class="ll-timing-note">The word timings are reviewed ASR estimates for this sample. They demonstrate the listening interface; they do not measure the original study-text alignment pipeline.</p>
</section>
<section class="ll-recordings" aria-labelledby="ll-recording-title">
  <div class="ll-recording-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The source interface, recorded</p><h2 id="ll-recording-title">The same small<br /><em>piece of listening.</em></h2><p>These genuine recordings show the original listening interface with this fictional sample. The player above retains its waveform and timed text, with a small static adapter for this page.</p></div>
  <div class="ll-films">
    <figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/media/listening/desktop.webp" width="1440" height="900" aria-label="Actual desktop listening workflow with recorded browser sound" aria-describedby="ll-desktop-description"><source src="/media/listening/desktop.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/media/listening/desktop.vtt" srclang="en" label="English actions" default />Your browser does not support video. <a href="/media/listening/desktop.mp4">Download the desktop recording.</a></video><figcaption id="ll-desktop-description"><strong>Desktop, with sound.</strong> Actual playback and current-word changes, waveform seeking, mouse region selection, phrase repetition, loop off, clear, zoom and keyboard controls. The soundtrack is captured browser output.</figcaption><details class="ll-film-description"><summary>What happens in the desktop recording</summary><p>The 24.23-second recording starts the AI-generated Danish story. A click seeks to a later moment. A mouse drag marks a region around “Koppen var tom, men under den lå et kort.” The interface repeats it, pauses at the region end when looping is disabled, then clears the region and zooms. Keyboard controls are exercised at the end. English action captions describe the workflow; the full original story is available above. Seeking and looping change which parts are heard.</p></details></figure>
    <figure class="ll-touch-film"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/media/listening/touch.webp" width="390" height="844" aria-label="Actual touch-emulated listening workflow, silent recording" aria-describedby="ll-touch-description"><source src="/media/listening/touch.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/media/listening/touch.vtt" srclang="en" label="English actions" default />Your browser does not support video. <a href="/media/listening/touch.mp4">Download the touch recording.</a></video><figcaption id="ll-touch-description"><strong>Touch emulation, silent.</strong> A tap seeks; an early drag cancels selection. A deliberate hold and drag marks a loop, followed by repeat, clear, zoom and a view change. Chromium mobile emulation at 390 × 844; no physical iPad was used.</figcaption><details class="ll-film-description"><summary>What happens in the touch recording</summary><p>The 17.88-second silent recording uses actual browser touch input. An ordinary tap moves the playhead without selecting a region. Moving before the hold threshold leaves the selection empty. A 550 ms hold arms selection; dragging then marks the phrase. Playback crosses the selected end and returns twice. Clear removes the region, zoom changes the waveform scale, and the settings drawer switches reading views. The captions describe these visible actions.</p></details></figure>
  </div>
</section>
<slot name="after-recordings" />
<details class="ll-provenance"><summary>What this demonstration includes <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div><article><h3>The actual components</h3><p>The waveform selection, touch threshold, loop boundaries, zoom and HTML-audio-driven timed views come from Saturation Listening’s actual components. Their original TypeScript source is retained and deterministically compiled for this route.</p><p>The page adapter supplies one static fixture, in-memory reading settings, scoped keyboard controls and the portfolio’s SVG icons. The keyboard sentence button sends a declared synthetic gesture through the actual waveform handlers; it is not described as trusted pointer input.</p><a class="text-link" href="/media/listening/receipt.json" download>Read the public receipt <Icon name="arrow-down" /></a></article><article><h3>One original fixture</h3><p>Original fictional text, AI-generated Cedar speech and real PCM waveform peaks. Independent CPU transcription recovered all 39 source words in order after punctuation and case normalization. Timing estimates were reviewed for this sample, with three declared overrides.</p><p>No original study corpus, progress database or server is used. This demonstrates playback and interaction, without a claim about learning outcomes, original PDF/SRT alignment accuracy, physical touch testing or human listening review.</p><p class="ll-license-links"><a href="/media/listening/notice.txt">Fixture and source notice</a> · <a href="/media/listening/react-license.txt">React</a> · <a href="/media/listening/react-dom-license.txt">React DOM</a> · <a href="/media/listening/scheduler-license.txt">Scheduler</a></p><span class="ll-source-revision">Source components: {provenance.source_revision.slice(0, 12)}</span></article></div></details>
<script>import './mount';</script>
